# The name is a leftover: this used to check that we reported no
# modseq. We support CONDSTORE now, so RFC7162 3.1.8 requires
# HIGHESTMODSEQ here, and [NOMODSEQ] would be wrong.
depends login
send 1
c select inbox (condstore)
receive 9
* 0 EXISTS
* 0 RECENT
* OK [UIDNEXT 1] next uid
* OK [HIGHESTMODSEQ 1] next modseq - 1
* FLAGS (\Answered \Deleted \Draft \Flagged \Seen)
* OK [PERMANENTFLAGS (\Answered \Deleted \Draft \Flagged \Seen \*)] permanent flags
* OK [UIDVALIDITY 1] uid validity
* OK [MAILBOXID (f...)] stable mailbox ID
c OK [READ-WRITE] done
end
